:: Bad Boy Saturn {"position":"1100,1375","size":"100,100"}
<h2>An example of hard-aspected natal Saturn:</h2>

''Suppose natal Saturn is:''

* Saturn 10° Aries
* square Moon 10° Cancer
* opposite Mars 10° Libra

At the Saturn return, transiting Saturn reaches ~10° Aries.

It is therefore simultaneously:
* conjunct natal Saturn
* square natal Moon
* opposite natal Mars

The return literally reconstructs Saturn's natal aspect network in transit.

Theoretically, this implies hard times for most people.

[[🔙->transits]]


:: Connection {"position":"825,750","size":"100,100"}
''You:'' I'm trying to understand my connection to another person.

''Me:'' Okay, not to John Edwards the situation, but I'm guessing it's probably relating to one of the following:
* Why are you so 'into' this person?
* Why did you instantaneously dislike this person, even though they did ABSOLUTELY nothing to you?
* Why do you *haaate* this person, but everybody else insists they're cool and technically the two of you don't have a beef?
* Why can't you *quit* this person, despite EVERYTHING THAT HAS HAPPENED?
* Is this a fleeting infatuation or something more lasting and important?
* Can we make it together, as a team, until one of us dies, without being the cause or losing our minds?
* Are we better as friends or lovers?
* Is there something in this person's chart that makes them so unattracted to me, despite everything? Is my unrequited love doomed, or should I keep trying, and refuse to give up hope?
* Is it worth the fight?
* What's with this weird Oedipal yearning? (omg, that's a joke; settle down)
* Are we cosmically predestined to break up?
* Am I gay or is it astrology?
* Who were we to each other in a past life?
* Would I marry my dog if my dog was a human?
* Should I marry my dog, anyway?
* Why did we break up?
* How much am I at fault for everything going wrong in this dynamic?
* How can we actually make this work, by understanding the dynamics better?
* Someone said that Aries shouldn't be with Sagittarians, and that made me sad, cos i love my Sag.
* I'm wondering if synastry's assessment of our dynamic will match our own, reveal something new, be completely bogus, and/or be inanely vague.

You'll notice some of these questions are looking for prescriptive answers, whereas others are seeking descriptive answers. Some are approaching synastry as though it were a 3rd party arbitrator of cosmic destiny, the final judge and jury of whether a relationship is sufficiently valid or not. As I see it, only some of these will result in useful answers, as far as astrology is concerned.

''Many of these questions can be answered in mundane (i.e. non-astrological) ways:''
* Power dynamics. Let's always start there, cos why not? Maybe it's hot. Maybe it's pissing you off.
* Competition. Sometimes it's fun. Sometimes it sucks.
* Biological selection & Darwinistic principles. Sometimes it's a smell thing, honestly. Sometimes it's symmetry. Sometimes someone is almost universally agreed upon as a 10 or a 3 within a given culture, and pretty much everyone feels this way; that doesn't say anything about *your* relationship, that says something about that person vs society.
* Early life imprinting & modeling by authority figures, caretakers and peers.
* Pattern recognition. Subconscious biases formed based on prior life experiences to always associate thing 1 with thing 2, and this person is activating that association in one or many ways, despite potentially limited knowledge of the person.
* It depends on how committed both of you are to each other, to the same goals, to the same vision for your relationship, and the resources available or potentially available to pursue these goals. And the extent to which you share common value systems, and how important those values are to each of you (as to whether discrepancies are a dealbreaker).
* Yes, you should marry your dog.

Which begs the question, if these questions can be answered through concrete observable reality, why bother with all the extra fuss of looking for any kind of metaphyiscal explanations, let alone surrendering to it as though it were destiny?

Personally, I think it's cool how some of these things appear to correlate strongly with people's natal charts, synastry and transits - stuff like power dynamics, instant attraction, seemingly innate value systems that might conflict with broader society and family/peers, and the selective perception of patterns in one's environment - the importance placed on some over others. But I like information for information's sake, and arguably, these correlations are superfluous in the broader scheme to functioning in reality. Also, if they are descriptive, cool - are they predictive? (That's what I've been testing, and it seems like, in many cases, yes, as far as I can tell - but definitely not all).

I also think the astrological factor supplies some valid factors that are otherwise unexplained in the dynamic between two people. It's unclear the degree to which they are more or less important than most any other single factor, aside from the absolute dealbreakers like genetics (lookin' at you, Oedipus)/sexuality/age/etc.

[[Theories]]


