:: Skeptic {"position":"975,750","size":"100,100"}
''You:'' I don't believe your silly app or star stuff nearly as much as I believe in certain dynamics between certain people, and I'm wondering the degree to which this app will Barnum effect / gaslight me about the nature of reality, on a scale of //Gulag Archipelago// to //Cosmo Magazine//

''Me:'' Hard agree.
And I'm admitting that from the perspective of someone who began attempting to debunk astrology using synastry first, as the easiest target. It was actually a sun-sign driven 20+ year marriage pairing correlation study I conducted from ~2008-2011 that led me to make this app, because I found unexpectedly strong correlations between certain Sun sign pairs, and evidence that some sun signs were radically underrepresented as ever having been married for 20 years in the first place. I evaluated approximately 400 couples, but I'd done the research so casually, for my own edification, that I couldn't easily validate the unexpected findings. This more or less set me on my current ongoingquest to determine the ways in which astrology is fully bogus, vs the ways in which its gaussian noise (eroneous correlations), vs the ways in which - if any - there's any validity to it. I've personally found some validity to it, but the subjective nature of interpretations makes it an admittedly tricky subject. And one way in which I've found it is unpredictable is exactly who is into who. The best predictor of that? Ask a person.

I say that, even while my Traits Predictor and several of the other Predictor modules in the app seems to work quite well, with regard to people I know personally enough to form any kind of opinion on the matter.

Why is Synastry so bogus, then?
I've been analyzing it, and have some theories.
