:: Soul Mate {"position":"712.5,625","size":"100,100"}
So you're looking for a soul mate.

I'm not going to tell you soul mates do or don't exist; we're both obviously entitled to our own opinions on the matter. We could, if you desire, examine [[some underpinnings such an idea might supply->What are Soulmates?]].

However, in an effort to be responsible, I should present this:
The quest for love, like many undertakings in life, can be equally impeded by  
1) an excess of trust (lack of critical thought, a failure to question motives and evidence, and to treat small samples of evidence of proof of what one wishes to believe), as 
2) a lack of trust (the obstinate tendency to always doubt one's own perceptions, regardless of an increasing body of evidence).

Yet the relentless seeking, the willingness to question and explore suggests a noble spirit, I think. And if you came here with such a spirit, to see what you might learn rather than to take what was presented as a new received wisdom, then you're in the right place. Let's look at what emerges from this experiment, without immediately leaping to ascribe a certain determinism to the results.

(If you love someone, and your charts predict friction, don't have a meltdown over it. There could well be a good reason for both, and arguably neither predicts the failure or success of a relationship in isolation.)

[[Thoughts on Synastry; how it works and how it doesn't->Synastry Definition]]


:: Synastry Definition {"position":"975,1000","size":"100,100"}
''What is Synastry?''
Synastry is a branch of astrology that examines how two natal charts engage one another by default. It is theoretically a model for baseline psychological/energetic chemistry.

In standard tropical (aka "Western") astrology, synastry charts are traditionally created by making a composite of two natal charts and seeing what 'aspects' form between their various sign-body positions.

Traditionally, in all common astrological canons, this is a [[dyadic]] model.

Some people conflate the idea of synastry with any/all of the following:
* compatibility
* instant attraction
* potential attraction
* whether the person is a 'soul mate'
* predicted longevity/stability of and/or 'happiness' within a relationship

''My thoughts:''
I think if there is any validity to it (and I now believe there is some), that what it is predicting specifically resembles:
* the kinds of obstacles and advantages two people tend to encounter in expressing themselves to one another
* the kinds of nonverbal tension and/or ease that seems inevitable and inexplicable at once
* potential conflicts in basic worldview and goals/values (albeit hugely culturally/peer-influenced in many cases, as well; I think a good synastry chart might set people up well to overcome these issues)
* a predictor of instant or slow-build attraction, pending supporting demographic factors (like age, gender/sexuality-compatibility, etc.)
* possibly, in some cases, for certain kinds of people, a sense of 'destiny' to the relationship, well before they ever knew each other's birth circumstances to project onto it. Maybe you finish each other's sentences. Maybe there's a freakish pileup of Jungian sychronicity blowing your mind every day. For a couple of Pisces stelliums, maybe they're telepathic and love Disco Elysium, for a couple of Aries-Sag-Taurus folks, maybe they both love pickleball and no one else can get them to shut up about itt.
* the degree to which someone reminds you of your ex
* the likelihood which you're going to date this person, given the opportunity/situational appropriateness

''''And individual natal charts seem pretty good at predicting:''''
* the likelihood of shared interests
* the likelihood of shared emotional responses to similar stimuli
* certain proclivities and mannerisms in relating to others

''What it definitely doesn't do:''
* predict whether or not a relationship is going to 'last' until the end of time in its current configuration, or at all. 
* predict whether the feeling is mutual or safe to express
* predict the ethics, wisdom, life stage, personal resources or relationship readiness of anyone involved
* predict the cultural norms either party may have around what to do with feelings of attraction, love and romance, or gender roles within a relationship.

