:: Theories {"position":"1100,875","size":"100,100"}
''In that case, let's consider a model of how Synastry could actually work in the real world:''

Astrology's basic model of Synastry is a [[dyadic]] model, and that is--in my opinion--its biggest flaw.
Like so many elements of astrological lore (and most pop metaphysics / 'new age' / 'woOo' frameworks), the common model of synastry is a really shallow, diluted conceptualization of reality.

Realistically, relationships are made up of many more components than the dynamic between two natal charts. To really understand what impacts a relationship (even just astrologically), we should be examining:

* [[The synastry chart: interaction between two natal charts->Synastry Definition]], yes
* [[The individual natal charts themselves->Natal Charts in Synastry]]
* [[The transits of each individual chart and the //global// transit->transits]].
* [[The charts of those in their immediate environment.->Interpersonal Context]]
* [[Demographic, cultural and socieconomicfactors->Mundane factors]]


