:: parasocial obsession {"position":"525,1125","size":"100,100"}
Listen, bud...

It might be useful to look into something called "psychological projection". 
It is literally impossible to truly and completely know someone you've never personally interacted with. Even if you managed to spy on them on uncurated, unguarded, unauthorized private moments for days or months or years on end, that would only supply you with a part of the puzzle, and never fully secure an answer to how they would perceive you, or how your chemistry and self-presentation would interact with their subconscious biases and conscious preferences/values in such a way that would make "love at first sight" anything approaching a sustainable or mutually rewarding relationship.

And that said, the vast majority of parasocial relationships are //highly// curated, based on someone's public/contextual persona, which turns out to be a very limited working knowledge of the individual's actual makeup, in most circumstances.

Perhaps this grants you access to a facet of them which you appreciate, but it's always useful to bear in mind that the curated self is often designed explicitly with the goal to be charming/attractive to others. The target audience may be broad or narrow, but regardless, the person is generally aware of some audience and is targeting their affections as a performance.

The performance of the self is not the self. It is not not-the-self, but merely a facet. And not always continuously sustainable in the day to day life one tends to experience in a long term intimate relationship with someone.

There's also the combined possibility that a person may project an excess of 'kismet'-coded feelings onto another they barely know out of:
* loneliness, a yearning for companionship, intimacy
* an affection for the idea of love, and/or 'romance' as a personal ideal/goal
* the desire to feel cared for, and that person was kind to you
* the desire to be kind to someone, and this person makes you feel especially sympathetic

Any of these things can feel like some version of 'love' but none of them are 'love' in the conventional sense. They are no less valid for that. They are simply something else that ought not be conflated. The confusion can be disappointing and frustrating.

[[Want to analyze it through a synastry lens, anyway?->Synastry Definition]]


:: transits {"position":"1100,1250","size":"100,100"}
''The impact of transits on synastry:''
For our purposes, it is useful to distinguish two ways of looking at transits:

''Global Transits''
The current geocentric positions and relationships of astronomical/astrological bodies at a given time—the astrological "weather" shared broadly by everyone and everything on Earth in that moment. 
If houses and angles are calculated, location also becomes relevant.

''Personal Transits''
A personal transit chart overlays the natal chart with the global transits for a particular moment. Technically this is not a composite chart; it is a natal-transit comparison. Conceptually, however, it is effectively the synastry between entity and spacetime coordinates.

It should be obvious without specifying how timing (time and place) tend to effect outcomes in any number of ways, not the least of which includes interpersonal dynamics.

Meet someone 10 years before the divorce, that might be awkward. Meet someone the day after the divorce, might still be awkward. Meet someone before you ever got married, or long after it's over, that's potentially a different relationship outcome altogether.

''Some subtle but salient notes on transits:''
Everyone's chart has certain patterns in it based on the cycles of 'astral weather'. Certain types of transit are universal within a lifetime, provided one lives long enough to experience them:

* Solar return: effectively the astrological birthday—the exact moment each year when the Sun returns to its natal longitude (which may or may not correspond exactly with the calendar birthday for various reasons).
* Lunar return: roughly every 27.3 days. Reset of the short-term lunar cycle: emotions, habits, needs, home, belonging and instinctive responses.
* Saturn return, Saturn waxing square, Saturn opposition, Saturn waning square, 
* Nodal return: aka Rahu/Ketu return, every ~18.6 years.
* Jupiter return: every ~11.9 years. Beginning of a new growth cycle.
* Mars return: every 2ish years. Reset of initiative, desire, assertion, competition, physical effort. Beginning of a new 'action cycle'. 

But people will theoretically experience these very differently depending on how that body is aspected within their natal charts, and the same can be said for most transits, broadly.

And it's worth noting that some people might feel something akin to these various cycles more frequently, depending on how many points of contact the associated body (i.e. Mars) has to other prominent chart elements (especially faster moving ones like Mercury or the Moon). 

''Examples:''
Per the lore, Chart A is getting his ass kicked by Saturn squares, oppositions and quincunxes. Saturn return is likely to crank up that energy while its transiting. Perhaps especially if the Global Transit of Saturn is already poorly aspected to begin with (i.e. [[a case when the global transit of Saturn has a bunch of hard aspects->Bad Boy Saturn]], as well).

Chart B has a great relationship with Saturn, it sort of just maxes out productivity, lends itself to a sense of permanence. That's Chart B's day to day relationship with Saturn. Her Saturn return is generally expected to be more chill/helpful, even if broadly the Global Transit of Saturn is negatively aspected. Though, per the model, other simultaneous transits can substantially alter the experience.

Chart B has Mars aspecting *lots* of bodies/planets, so those transits may also activate the natal Mars relationship, and it may feel like a mini-action cycle gets kicked off, providing a very energizing effect.

''Is that real?''
I've been trying to figure that out. It seems to track pretty well, but that's subjective, very difficult to quantify. I'm in the process of building additional models to track it blindly and with controls and see what turns up, if anything of value. Until then, I can't assert these astrological claims as any kind of fact or something I definitely endorse personally as the developer, but my personal experience with the overlap between claim and experienced phenomena was sufficient that I deemed further, more empirical testing worthwhile.

