:: why is this a thing {"position":"1025,625","size":"100,100"}
Sometimes when two people share a kind of bond, it can be extremely puzzling to outsiders, especially outsiders who have never experienced that kind of bond themselves, or don't necessarily understand one or both of the parties involved.

If you're making a synastry chart to try to understand what the heck is going on with such a pair, that's possibly a useful first step. Provided that both sets of birth data are correct/complete (including time and place) and you seek interpretation of the results through reputable sources, I do personally think you will find some relevant and potentially useful answers in your synastry analysis.

That said, there are many other factors in why two people understand each other that must also be considered, and I don't think it would be responsible to present this particular tool (which many people approach with a certain religious fervor) without including more mundane alternatives, a few of which include:

* Shared life experiences
* Shared cultural/demographic background
* Shared peer groups
* Transactional desire/necessity (one  has something the other needs or wants, which may say more about one party or the other than their specific dynamic as a pair? Though likely has a lot to do with at least 2-3 of those factors)

Nonetheless, it's possible that the synastry chart may even predict some of these factors in terms of the sort of dynamic that arises between two people. I'm not sure. In the interest of being scientific, it's impossible to say that anything approaching destiny or fate is governed by anything resembling 'cosmic forces', while it arguably remains difficult to assert with great conviction that no such factor impacts the trajectory of a life or relationships therein.

That's just my personal unsolicited opinion.

Does astrology have any predictive/descriptive or persuasive power over factors such as power dynamics between two given people? What about groups?
I made this app in an effort to answer those sorts of questions, so let's venture forth discovering new findings together, while studiously avoiding any hasty assumptions as much as possible.

[[Current theories of synastry->Theories]]
